<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bertrand of Saint-Geniès</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1260–<a href="/years/1350">1350</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Bertrand de Saint-Geniès</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bertrand of Saint-Geniès was a French churchman who served as Patriarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aquileia">Aquileia</a> from 1334 to 1350. He worked to restore the patriarchate's authority in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friuli">Friuli</a> against the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorizia">Gorizia</a> and rebellious nobles, and to reform its clergy. He was murdered by Friulian nobles near Spilimbergo in 1350 and was later beatified.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bertrand-of-saint-genies.jpg" alt="Bertrand of Saint-Geniès" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: YukioSanjo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:5324_-_Duomo_di_Udine_-_Teca_con_corpo_Beato_Bertrando_di_San_Genesio.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
